{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/pulls/2187","id":4960774905,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAivEQM8AAAABJ69q-Q","html_url":"https://github.com/osfans/trime/pull/2187","diff_url":"https://github.com/osfans/trime/pull/2187.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/osfans/trime/pull/2187.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/issues/2187","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/pulls/2187/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/pulls/2187/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/issues/2187/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/statuses/7f909060a1d42198e749eb1f9a66399f76bf8710","number":2187,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(ime): keep candidate text in sync with TextView layout","user":{"login":"X2M7","id":239118790,"node_id":"U_kgDODkCpxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/239118790?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7","html_url":"https://github.com/X2M7","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Candidate labels can disappear during accessibility-node inspection when custom drawing uses private text while the framework TextView still has an empty text/layout. Keep framework text as the single value and synchronize its Layout before the existing custom sizing/scaling. This PR changes one production file.\n\nReview follow-up in `92b13711`:\n\n- Set our dirty flags before the parent setter; restrict our explicit layout/redraw requests to changed content or null. Always forward the original nullable text and BufferType to `super.setText`: the parent constructor calls this override, and equal text can still need NORMAL/SPANNABLE/EDITABLE conversion.\n- Remove the added `super.onLayout` call.\n- Retain `super.onMeasure` with a comment explaining its framework Layout/accessibility role. In the separately compiled API21 source controls, removing it leaves the first 11 Layout checks failing while their reference passes; the later two selectable/granularity checks pass. Putting the entire setter inside the suggested equality guard instead aborts during initial `BoringLayout.isBoring` measurement, before buffer tests, with no exported result.\n\nValidation of this head:\n\n- [Exact-source control](https://github.com/X2M7/trime/actions/runs/39872481596): 301 existing application JVM tests actually executed, zero failures/errors/skips. [Fork CI](https://github.com/X2M7/trime/actions/runs/39872383227): 4/4 jobs; [upstream PR CI](https://github.com/osfans/trime/actions/runs/39872386788): 5/5. Four original Ubuntu ABI APKs are audited; upstream synthetic-merge artifacts are kept separate.\n- The unchanged, un-re-signed original x86_64 APK class passes 13 API21 stages / 39 PNGs: construction/Hanzi/Latin/null/rebind, six equal-content buffer sequences, and selectable/public LINE NEXT/PREVIOUS actions (`0 → 2 → 0`). Text, Layout, nodes, immediate buffer types and glyphs are checked against the same-stage reference.\n- API35 is **not qualified**: the safe diagnostic runs zero stages because its 8-second combined window-focus / shown-view / positive-width precondition fails; individual values were not recorded. SystemUI ANR precedes the probe and the restored screen shows its dialog, without proving a unique cause. Both negative controls and the original-APK phase remain unrun.\n\n[Sources, controls, original reports/screenshots and scoped qualification](https://github.com/X2M7/trime/tree/9eb3810a0a578b786e4d9cb92835a2c186f9073c/doc/contribution-split/checks/candidate-review-20261023) are outside this one-file patch. The external Activity loads the original installed class; this is not native IME/candidate activation, TalkBack-service, physical-device, Release, upgrade or performance acceptance. Source controls use their own diagnostic toolchain. Observed native dependency, SDK/Gradle/JDK and Debug META-INF/services signature warnings remain; no zero-warning or all-native-objects-rebuilt claim.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-22T01:37:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T02:21:33Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"9ff9572f2ed289d8af198f81ce08bdac66d8a69c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"X2M7:contrib/pr-candidate-text-layout","ref":"contrib/pr-candidate-text-layout","repo":{"id":1252010092,"node_id":"R_kgDOSqAobA","name":"trime","full_name":"X2M7/trime","owner":{"login":"X2M7","id":239118790,"node_id":"U_kgDODkCpxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/239118790?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7","html_url":"https://github.com/X2M7","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/events{/privacy}","received_e